    "mood": "tired",
    "titleEs": "Dormir también es confiar",
    "titleEn": "Sleeping is also trusting",
    "refEs": "Salmos 127:2",
    "refEn": "Psalms 127:2",
    "verseEs": "De nada les sirve levantarse temprano y acostarse tarde, comiendo el pan del sufrimiento; el Señor da a sus amados mientras duermen.",
    "verseEn": "It is vain for you to rise up early, to stay up late, eating the bread of toil, for he gives sleep to his loved ones.",
    "reflectionEs": "Este salmo se atribuye a Salomón y habla de que, si Dios no edifica la casa, en vano trabajan los que la construyen. El versículo 2 va más lejos: es inútil madrugar, trasnochar y comer con ansiedad el pan del esfuerzo, porque Dios da el sueño a los que ama. No es un elogio de la pereza. Es una invitación a reconocer que no sostienes el mundo.\n\nSi estás en época de exámenes, de trabajo pesado o de preocupaciones, acostarte a dormir es un acto de fe: dices que Dios sigue despierto y que lo que no terminaste hoy no se cae. Hoy apaga el celular una hora antes, entrega lo pendiente en oración y duerme. Descansar bien es parte de hacer bien las cosas.",
    "reflectionEn": "This psalm is attributed to Solomon and says that unless God builds the house, those who build it labor in vain. Verse 2 goes further: it is useless to rise early, stay up late and eat the bread of anxious toil, because God gives sleep to those he loves. It is not praise of laziness. It is an invitation to recognize that you do not hold up the world.\n\nIf you are in exam season, a heavy workload or a time of worry, lying down to sleep is an act of faith: you are saying God is still awake and that what you did not finish today will not fall apart. Tonight turn off your phone an hour earlier, hand over what is pending in prayer, and sleep. Resting well is part of doing things well.",
    "prayerEs": "Padre, lo que no terminé hoy te lo entrego. Tú no duermes ni te cansas. Dame un sueño tranquilo y fuerzas para mañana. Amén.",
    "prayerEn": "Father, what I did not finish today I hand to you. You neither sleep nor tire. Give me quiet sleep and strength for tomorrow. Amen.",
    "catEs": "Sueño",
    "catEn": "Sleep",
    "promiseRefEs": "Salmos 4:8",
    "promiseRefEn": "Psalms 4:8",
    "promisePassageEs": "«Me acostaré y descansaré en paz, porque solo tú, Señor, me mantienes a salvo.»",
    "promisePassageEn": "«In peace I will both lay myself down and sleep, for you alone, LORD, make me live in safety.»",
    "meditationEs": "David se acuesta en paz y se duerme, y da la razón: solo Dios lo hace vivir confiado. La seguridad no viene de que todo esté resuelto.",
    "meditationEn": "David lies down in peace and falls asleep, and gives the reason: only God makes him live in safety. Security does not come from everything being solved.",
    "declarationEs": "Descanso porque Dios cuida de mí.",
    "declarationEn": "I rest because God watches over me."
