    "mood": "peace",
    "titleEs": "Amar es algo que se hace",
    "titleEn": "Love is something you do",
    "refEs": "1 Corintios 13:4-5",
    "refEn": "1 Corinthians 13:4-5",
    "verseEs": "El amor es paciente y bondadoso. El amor no tiene envidia. El amor no se jacta ni se llena de orgullo. No se porta indebidamente, no busca lo suyo, no se irrita, no guarda rencor.",
    "verseEn": "Love is patient and is kind. Love doesn’t envy. Love doesn’t brag, is not proud, doesn’t behave itself inappropriately, doesn’t seek its own way, is not provoked, takes no account of evil.",
    "reflectionEs": "Pablo escribe esto a una iglesia dividida, con egos grandes y poca paciencia. Por eso no define el amor como un sentimiento, sino como una lista de verbos y de actitudes: es paciente, es bondadoso, no guarda rencor. Lo que describe se puede entrenar, no solo sentir.\n\nSi estás en una relación de pareja, de amistad o de familia, pasa esa lista por un solo día. ¿Fui paciente cuando me molestó? ¿Guardé la cuenta de lo que me deben? No para castigarte, sino para ver con claridad. Hoy elige una actitud de la lista y practícala con una persona concreta. El amor que dura casi nunca se basa en cómo me siento, sino en lo que decido hacer.",
    "reflectionEn": "Paul writes this to a divided church, with big egos and little patience. That is why he does not define love as a feeling, but as a list of verbs and attitudes: it is patient, it is kind, it keeps no record of wrongs. What he describes can be trained, not only felt.\n\nIf you are in a relationship, a friendship or a family, run that list through a single day. Was I patient when I was bothered? Did I keep score of what I am owed? Not to punish yourself, but to see clearly. Today choose one attitude from the list and practice it with a specific person. Love that lasts is almost never based on how I feel, but on what I decide to do.",
    "prayerEs": "Padre, enséñame a amar con hechos y no solo con palabras. Dame paciencia con quien me cuesta y humildad para pedir perdón. Amén.",
    "prayerEn": "Father, teach me to love with actions and not only with words. Give me patience with the one who is hard for me and humility to ask forgiveness. Amen.",
    "catEs": "Pareja",
    "catEn": "Relationships",
    "promiseRefEs": "Efesios 4:2",
    "promiseRefEn": "Ephesians 4:2",
    "promisePassageEs": "«Anden con toda humildad y mansedumbre, con paciencia, soportándose unos a otros en amor.»",
    "promisePassageEn": "«with all lowliness and humility, with patience, bearing with one another in love.»",
    "meditationEs": "Pablo une la humildad, la mansedumbre y la paciencia para soportarse con amor. Una relación sana no es la que no tiene roces, sino la que sabe sostenerlos.",
    "meditationEn": "Paul joins humility, gentleness and patience to bear with one another in love. A healthy relationship is not one without friction, but one that knows how to hold it.",
    "declarationEs": "Elijo amar con paciencia y con hechos.",
    "declarationEn": "I choose to love with patience and with actions."
